{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1176274-question-about-the-chimera-background-specifically-items","id":1176274,"title":"Question about the Chimera Background (Specifically Items)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-15T07:24:41-08:00","id":1176274,"title":"Question about the Chimera Background (Specifically Items)","content":"I was hoping someone here might be able to answer a question regarding the Chimera Background, specifically items. I was searching trying to find an answer, but was struggling to find a good one. The rules for creating a Chimera Companion are pretty solid in the Chimera section. And they have good rules for crafting a Chimera item. However, they do nothing to indicate what different levels of Chimera items mean. I have a friend who wants to take Chimera 5 for a weapon, for his character. The background states that this should be a legendary item, but with no rules attacked to that,, if feels like that just means &quot;Its ST discretion&quot; on what a legendary item is. Since Treasures are specifically magical, I'm assuming Chimera Items are not. My only guess is to give it better stats than a normal weapon, and have some &quot;social&quot; affects from him having it. I wanted to check here though, and see if anyone could provide an answer on, just what a 5 point Chimera weapon should be and if there are actual rules for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T15:46:40-08:00","id":1176399,"title":"","content":"Kithbook Nicker is the book to go for that, I'm overseas so can't check in details, but basically, you're looking at stuff like exoskeleton that gives bonus strength/soak, chimerical lasers, aircraft etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T20:41:12-08:00","id":1176451,"title":"","content":"There doesn't currently seem to be anything similar for C20 but for CtD 2nd ed there was a chart in the core book on p288 that gives some examples of chimera costs for various items. Generally speaking, a good one-handed weapon is about a 2 dot background, anything requiring two hands is about 3 dots. Anything higher seems to have some Art associated with it (ie, it's a magic item). The same page suggests a character could be allowed to have multiple items at about the same or lower tier without purchasing a separate background, up to ST discretion but only one magical item.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if the knocker book has better info, I don't think I ever read that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23656-lanir","name":"Lanir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}